meta {
  name: 72 EMI Panel Flow E2E
  seq: 72
}

script:pre-request {
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // EMI PANEL Flow E2E — folder-level setup (runs before every request here).
  //
  // Same shape as "71 EMI Machine Flow E2E", but the order carries a LAB PANEL
  // with TWO member tests instead of a single standalone test. This exercises the
  // panel path of the EMI endpoints: a panel is one OrderItem (branchLabPanelId
  // set, branchLabTestId NULL) whose member tests live on the per-member
  // LabReport rows as `memberBranchLabTestId` — the key the adapter is mapped on.
  //
  //   bootstrap (siteadmin → tenant → branch → operator) →
  //   catalogue: TWO lab tests (each WITH a result parameter) → import both →
  //   build a PANEL of the two → import the panel into the branch →
  //   order the panel → accession bulk-collect + bulk-ACCEPT (creates one report
  //     per member test) →
  //   register the machine (siteadmin equipment + business lab adapter mapping
  //     BOTH member branch lab tests → token) →
  //   MACHINE scan (/emi/orders): ut_ids carry BOTH members from the single panel
  //     barcode → MACHINE submit (/emi/submitResult) fills BOTH member reports →
  //   verify both values landed (source = ADAPTER, status = SAVED).
  //
  // Every id/token is captured by each request's post-response via
  // bru.setVar(...) — nothing is copied by hand. Just Run Folder, or click Next.
  // A per-run unique id (panelRunId) keeps unique fields from colliding on re-runs
  // and is namespaced separately from flow 71 so both can run in one session.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  if (!bru.getVar("baseUrl"))    bru.setVar("baseUrl", "http://localhost:3000/api/v1");
  // EMI endpoints live at the ROOT (not under /api/v1) — host only.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiBaseUrl")) bru.setVar("emiBaseUrl", "http://localhost:3000");

  // Entry point — the SEEDED platform SiteAdmin (prisma/seed.ts). The ONLY
  // credential this flow assumes exists; the tenant + business admin are created
  // at runtime. Change these two only if your seeded SiteAdmin differs.
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminEmail"))    bru.setVar("siteAdminEmail", "admin@kalnostics.com");
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("siteAdminPassword", "SuperSecret1");

  // Known passwords this flow sets (so every login is automated).
  if (!bru.getVar("operatorPassword"))       bru.setVar("operatorPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");
  if (!bru.getVar("bootstrapAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("bootstrapAdminPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");

  // TWO analytes — one per panel member test. Each `emiParamCode*` is sent as the
  // machine's `universal_test_id` and must equal the `parameterCode` created on
  // its member lab test (steps 14/15); each `emiParamName*` is that member's
  // `parameterName`, which appears in the scan's `ut_ids`.
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeA"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeA", "HGB");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameA"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameA", "Hemoglobin");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitA"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitA", "g/dL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueA")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueA", "13.5");

  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamCodeB"))   bru.setVar("emiParamCodeB", "WBC");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamNameB"))   bru.setVar("emiParamNameB", "WBC Count");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiParamUnitB"))   bru.setVar("emiParamUnitB", "10^3/uL");
  if (!bru.getVar("emiResultValueB")) bru.setVar("emiResultValueB", "7.2");

  // One-time per-run unique suffix + derived unique mobiles (namespaced `panel*`
  // so this flow never clobbers flow 71's vars if both are run in one session).
  if (!bru.getVar("panelRunId")) {
    const n = String(Date.now());
    bru.setVar("panelRunId", n.slice(-6));
    // 10-digit national mobiles (^\d{10}$) — distinct prefixes from flow 71.
    bru.setVar("panelAdminPhone",     "93" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("panelOperatorMobile", "92" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("panelPatientMobile",  "91" + n.slice(-8));
  }
}

docs {
  # EMI Panel Flow E2E — the analyzer integration, with a 2-test lab panel

  A sibling of **71 EMI Machine Flow E2E**. It reproduces the exact same
  lab-analyzer round-trip (same `TOKEN` header, GET-with-`text/plain`-body, flat
  `{ s, m, … }` responses), but the order carries a **lab panel of two member
  tests** instead of one standalone test. This proves the EMI endpoints resolve a
  scanned **panel** barcode down to its member tests.

  ## Why a panel is different
  A panel is stored as **one `OrderItem`** with `branchLabPanelId` set and
  `branchLabTestId = NULL`. Accession expands it into **one accession sample per
  member test**, and acceptance creates **one `LabReport` per member test**, each
  tagged with `memberBranchLabTestId` (a `BranchLabTest.id`). The adapter is
  mapped on those **member** branch lab tests — so `/emi/orders` must expand the
  panel and `/emi/submitResult` must fill each member report.

  ## How to run
  Select this folder and **Run Folder**, or click **Next**. Each request captures
  the ids/tokens the next one needs via `bru.setVar(...)`. A `panelRunId` is
  generated once per run so re-runs never collide. The only credential assumed to
  exist is the **seeded SiteAdmin** (`admin@kalnostics.com` / `SuperSecret1`).

  ## Flow
  **Bootstrap:** 01 SiteAdmin login → 02 create tenant + business admin → 03
  business-admin login → 04 branch (enables `accession`) → 05 operating schedule →
  06 operator user → 08 grant the operator collect + accept → 09 operator login.

  **Catalogue + panel:** 12 patient → 13 resolve branch master data → **14/15 two
  lab tests**, each created by the Business Admin WITH a `resultParams` entry
  (`HGB`, `WBC`) so its report is fillable → **16 import BOTH into the branch**
  (walk-in list) → 17/18 resolve `branchLabTestIdA` / `branchLabTestIdB` → **19
  create a lab panel of the two tests** → **20 import the panel into the branch**
  (its members REUSE the two branch lab tests imported in 16) → 21 resolve
  `branchLabPanelId`.

  **Order + accept:** 22 create the order with the **panel** as its single item →
  23 list accession samples (**two** samples — one per member — sharing **one
  barcode** under the default Dept+Sample grouping) → **24 bulk-collect** →
  **25 bulk-accept** (creates the two member `LabReport`s, PENDING).

  **Register the machine:** 26 SiteAdmin equipment → **27 lab adapter mapping
  BOTH member branch lab tests** → captures `flowAdapterToken`.

  **Machine talks to us:** **28 `GET /emi/orders`** — one scan of the panel
  barcode returns `ut_ids` carrying **both** members (`Hemoglobin` + `WBC Count`
  and their test names) → **29 `GET /emi/submitResult`** submits **both** analyte
  values in one call.

  **Logged (three scopes):** 30 branch / 31 business / 32 site-admin adapter-logs
  reads — the same as flow 71.

  **Verify both members filled:** 33 list the panel's reports
  (`?branchLabPanelId=`) — **two** reports, both `SAVED` → 34/35 each report's
  detail carries an `ADAPTER`-sourced value (`13.5` and `7.2`).

  > This is the panel counterpart of the single-test flow 71: **one panel barcode
  > → both member tests in `ut_ids` → both member reports filled from one submit.**
}
